  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Peaceful, Safe, Sustainable Reintegration Support for Returning Migrants and Host Communities in Zimbabwe Impacted by the Non-renewal of the Zimbabwe Exemption Permit (ZEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to provide capacity strengthening support to Government of Zimbabwe and Civil Society Organizations in migration management and conflict prevention, and to facilitate social cohesion, assistance and sustainable reintegration of Zimbabwe returnees impacted by the non-renewal of the ZEP to prevent conflict in the receiving hosting communities. The project seeks to achieve the following outcomes: 1. Strengthened capacity of GoZ, CSOs and Diaspora associations in migration management and conflict prevention to assist returning migrants and vulnerable populations in receiving host communities; 2. Returning migrants and receiving communities have sufficient level of economic self-sufficiency, social stability, and psychosocial wellbeing; and 3. Increased access to protection services and improved documentation of protection needs.</narrative>
  </description>
